diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..287ab50
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+# Demand forecasting module - implementation notes
+
+**Not executed.** There was no PHP or database available while writing this, so none of it has been run. The SQL and PHP
+were written against the existing code and need a smoke test (new install, upgrade of an existing database, one pass
+through each page) before release.
+
+## What was built
+
+A **Forecasting** module (`modulelink` `forecast`, report link `fcst`) in the main menu, directly after Manufacturing.
+
+### Pages (all in the webERP root, helpers in `includes/ForecastFunctions.php`)
+
+| Page | Token | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ForecastDashboard.php` | 11 | Active forecasts / summary forecasts, history range, counts, links to every function |
+| `ForecastHistory.php` | 11 | Extract sales history for a range of months (replace, not add) |
+| `ForecastGenerate.php` | 11 | One item (one location or all combined) or every active item of a category; 12 methods or best fit; batch with progress and result list |
+| `ForecastReview.php` | 11 | Search forecasts, period by period calculated / revised / last year's actual / variance, enter or clear revisions |
+| `ForecastInquiry.php` | 11 | Read-only view by item, category, location, period (optionally superseded forecasts) |
+| `ForecastSummary.php`, `ForecastSummaryReview.php` | 11 | Summary forecasts by category, customer type, sales area, salesperson; review with the item detail behind each |
+| `ForecastAccuracy.php` | 11 | MAD, POA, MSE, RMSE per item, category and method for a range; low-accuracy flag |
+| `ForecastCompare.php` | 11 | One item, several methods side by side on held-out months |
+| `ForecastToMRP.php` | 11 | Convert active forecasts into MRP demands |
+| `ForecastParameters.php` | 15 | Company defaults (alpha, beta, gamma, season length, MA periods, hold-out, horizon, growth %, low-POA threshold, batch size) |
+
+Token 11 ("Inventory Management and Pricing") is what the Manufac/Stock Admin, Purchasing, AR Clerk, Accountant and
+System Administrator roles hold; the parameters page needs 15 (system administration). The menu also links the existing
+`MRPDemands.php` (master schedule), `MRP.php` (run) and `MRPReport.php`.
+
+### Objects (tables)
+
+`forecasthistory` (item, location, month, plus customer type / area / salesman of the invoice so summaries come from the
+same rows), `forecasts` + `forecastlines` (header with method, parameters, history range; one line per month with
+`calcqty` and nullable `revisedqty`), `forecastsummaries` + `forecastsummarylines`, `forecastparameters`,
+`forecastbatches` / `forecastbatchresults` / `forecastbatchfit` (batch state, per-item results, per-method errors for the
+category best fit). New column `mrpdemands.fromforecast`. New demand type `FCST` "Statistical Forecast".
+
+One active forecast per item and location is enforced by the database: `forecasts.activekey` is 1 while active and
+NULL once superseded, with a unique key on (stockid, loccode, activekey). Generating again supersedes (keeps the old
+row, method and parameters; its lines stay for accuracy measurement). Location `''` means "all locations combined".
+
+## Where the history comes from and how it reaches MRP
+
+* **History**: `stockmoves` of type 10 (sales invoice) and 11 (credit note / return) with `hidemovt = 0`, quantity sign
+  reversed, summed by item, location and calendar month of `trandate`. This is exactly what `InventoryPlanning.php`,
+  `StockUsage.php` and `SalesInquiry.php` count, so credits are deducted and open orders are not included. Re-extracting
+  deletes the months in the range and inserts them again in one transaction.
+* **MRP**: `ForecastToMRP.php` writes one `mrpdemands` row per item and forecast month (dated the first of the month,
+  type `FCST`, `fromforecast = 1`), using `COALESCE(revisedqty, calcqty)`. The existing `MRP.php` already loads every
+  `mrpdemands` row when "use MRP demands" is selected, so the planned purchase and work orders follow with no change to MRP.
+  * *Replace*: deletes `FCST` rows with `fromforecast = 1` for the items in scope whose date is inside the horizon, then inserts.
+  * *Incremental*: inserts only (item, month) pairs without such a row.
+  * Both run in one transaction, so converting twice never doubles. Rows without `fromforecast = 1` (hand entered, auto-created,
+    or typed by hand under the `FCST` type) are never deleted. `MRPDemandTypes.php` now refuses to create or delete `FCST`.
+
+## Integration with the rest of webERP
+
+* **Database for new installs**: `install/sql/tables/forecast*.sql`, `mrpdemands.sql` (new column), `www_users.sql`
+  (`modulesallowed` widened to 50), `install/sql/data/modules.sql` (Forecasting at sequence 7, later modules moved up),
+  `data/forecastscripts.sql`, `data/forecastmenuitems.sql`, `data/forecastdemandtype.sql`, `data/forecastparameters.sql`,
+  and the same rows appended to `install/sql/demo.sql` (done there with an UPDATE/INSERT..SELECT because the file is single-line dumps).
+* **Database for existing installs**: `sql/updates/44.php`, the project's `DBUpdateNumber` mechanism (a new install records 44
+  as already applied). It creates the tables, adds the column, seeds parameters and the demand type, registers the scripts with
+  their page security, inserts the module and the menu items.
+* **Existing users keep exactly their modules.** `www_users.modulesallowed` is a positional comma list matching the module
+  sequence, so inserting a module in the middle would silently hand every user the wrong modules. `44.php` inserts a `0` at
+  the new position in every user's list (`'1,1,1,1,1,1,1,...'` becomes `'1,1,1,1,1,1,0,1,...'`), after shifting the sequence of
+  General Ledger..Utilities by one. The administrator grants Forecasting per user in `WWW_Users.php` (new "Display Forecasting
+  module" row). The position is computed from the Manufacturing row, not hard coded. Customer and supplier login creation
+  (`CustLoginSetup.php`, `SuppLoginSetup.php`) now write 12 flags.
+* **Menu items** are inserted only for roles that hold the page's token (new installs: static rows; upgrade: a join on
+  `scripts.pagesecurity` and `securitygroups`). Every role still gets the module row, because the flag list is positional.
+  `index.php` was made tolerant of a role with no Transactions item in a module.
+* `Z_ChangeStockCode.php` also renames the stock code in the forecasting tables (they carry no foreign key on `stockid`,
+  because `stockmaster.stockid` is 20 characters on new installs and 64 on upgraded ones).
+* **Translations**: every visible string uses `__()`, including captions in `44.php`. `messages.pot` was **not** regenerated
+  (it is generated by the extraction tool); run it before translators start.
+
+## BRD points that were ambiguous, and what was decided
+
+1. **History month boundaries / current month.** Monthly buckets are calendar months of `trandate`. The last month cannot be later than
+   the last complete month (a part month would read as a collapse in demand); the page trims it and says so. The held history must stay
+   one continuous run: a new extract has to overlap or touch it, otherwise a gap would read as zero sales.
+2. **What "history length" is for the minimum-history rules.** From the item's first month with any sale up to the end of the held
+   history, with months without sales as zeros. Months before the first sale are not history (item may not have existed). Locations
+   are summed for "all locations".
+3. **POA.** Defined as 100 x (1 - total absolute error / total actual), floored at 0, rather than the JDE "forecast / actual"
+   ratio, which reads 100% when over- and under-forecasts cancel. Bias is not shown; flagged items are those below the
+   company threshold (default 70).
+4. **Several methods are only described by name.** Chosen definitions: method 1/3 use the same month last year, and beyond 12
+   months of horizon the forecast of the year before (so percent growth compounds); method 2 growth = last 12 months / the 12 before;
+   method 4 flat mean of the last N; method 5 a line through the month `span` months back (default 6) and the last month;
+   method 6/7 least squares over all history; method 8 the user's 12 weights on the prior 12 months, not normalised, applied
+   recursively; method 9 weights normalised to 1, most recent first (default 40/30/20/10), flat; 10 and 11 start from the first
+   months; 12 is additive Holt-Winters with season length 2-12 (minimum history stays 24). Smoothing constants must be 0.1-0.9.
+   Negative results are clamped to 0 and rounded to 2 decimals.
+5. **Hold-out for best fit.** The most recent `HoldoutMonths` (default 3) are held out; a method is tested only if the *training*
+   part meets its minimum history. Winner = lowest total absolute error (ties to the lower method number). For a category, the winner is the
+   method with the lowest total error relative to total sales, among methods testable on at least half of the items that could be
+   tested at all; items it cannot forecast are reported as failures with the reason (never forecast with invented data).
+6. **Which forecast counts for accuracy.** For an (item, location, month) the latest forecast covering that month is measured
+   (superseded forecasts are needed, they are the ones that cover months now sold); a checkbox measures every version.
+7. **Summary forecasts** are item-independent: the group's history (all items sold to that customer type / area / salesperson /
+   in that category, using the invoice's customer branch at extraction time and the item's current category) is forecast with the same
+   methods. They are not converted to MRP (MRP needs items).
+8. **MRP location.** `mrpdemands` has no location. If an item has an active all-locations forecast it is used; otherwise the active
+   per-location forecasts are summed. Months are dated the first of the month and converted when that date is inside the chosen
+   horizon. Replace mode clears forecast demands for every active item in scope (not only those with a forecast), so a forecast that no
+   longer exists cannot linger. Zero quantities are not written.
+9. **Batches** run in steps of `BatchSize` items per request, the page continuing itself, with the state kept in `forecastbatches`;
+   the best-fit category run has an evaluation pass and then a generation pass.
+10. **Access to the data.** The pages are gated by page security only; location restrictions (`locationusers`) are not applied
+    to the history, which is company-wide.
+
+## Not done / follow-ups
+
+* No automated tests; nothing was run.
+* `sql/demo.sql` (old full dump) and the legacy `UpgradeDatabase.php` / `sql/mysql/upgrade*.sql` path were left alone: they
+  predate the `sql/updates` mechanism. (That legacy switch also stops at `4.15`, an existing issue.)
+* Month labels use PHP `date('M Y')` and are not localised.
